# INACTIVE — Milestone 8 scaffold only.
#
# This file is not started by default: `deploy/compose.yaml`'s `caddy`
# service is behind the `webhook` Compose profile
# (`docker compose --profile webhook up -d`), which nothing in this
# milestone enables. It exists now so Milestone 8 (Plaid webhook, handoff
# §29) only has to fill in the actual route, not design reverse-proxy/TLS
# from scratch, and so `docs/deployment.md` can describe the full target
# topology today.
#
# When Milestone 8 lands:
#   - replace {$WEBHOOK_DOMAIN} with the owner-provisioned domain (handoff
#     §32 — a domain/DNS choice needing owner input);
#   - Caddy handles ACME/TLS automatically once a real domain resolves to
#     this host — no certificate material is ever checked into this repo;
#   - the webhook handler validates Plaid's webhook signature (handoff
#     §6.4) before ever touching sync state — reverse-proxy termination is
#     not a substitute for that application-level check;
#   - nothing else is exposed here. The CLI/chat/finops surface stays
#     SSH-only (handoff §5) and is never proxied.
{$WEBHOOK_DOMAIN:webhook.example.invalid} {
	reverse_proxy app:8080

	# Plaid signs webhook requests; validation happens in the app itself
	# (finance_app.plaid.webhook, Milestone 8). This proxy layer only
	# terminates TLS and forwards — it makes no trust decision.
	log {
		output stdout
		format json
	}
}
